# Design: Two default Codex roots, one watcher

## Problem
Codex moves ended rollouts from sessions/ into archived_sessions/.
Only sessions/ was watched, so archived rollouts were never ingested,
and a file moved there stopped being watched without any report.

## Approach
An agent root now carries a list of directories. The Codex agent gets
sessions/ (the --codex-root flag value) plus $CODEX_HOME/archived_sessions
(always optional). Both paths feed one watcher and one checkpoint file
per agent, so the existing move-by-file-identity rebind keeps the
checkpoint across a move between the roots. Missing watched sources now
print one diagnostic line per disappearance on both ingest and upload.

## Key Trade-offs
- The archived root is watched even when --codex-root is passed
  explicitly. ohya setup writes an explicit --codex-root into the
  service, so a conditional archived root would silently drop archived
  capture for every installed user.
- Watching all of ~/.codex was rejected: it would ingest
  session_index.jsonl, history.jsonl, and vendor JSONL.

